   "name": "How Your Car Mixes Fuel and Air",
   "lines": [
    [
     "c12_1",
     {
      "label": "hook",
      "head": "The perfect mix: *14.7 to 1*",
      "pose": "point",
      "face": "grin",
      "prop": {
       "type": "injector",
       "ratio": true
      }
     },
     "For petrol to burn cleanly, it needs about fourteen point seven parts air to one part fuel, by weight."
    ],
    [
     "c12_2",
     {
      "label": "old",
      "head": "Old cars used *carburettors*",
      "pose": "shrug",
      "face": "smug",
      "prop": {
       "type": "tags",
       "items": [
        "CARBURETTOR",
        "NOT PRECISE",
        "CHOKE ON COLD DAYS"
       ]
      }
     },
     "Older cars used a carburettor, which let airflow suck fuel in. Simple, but not very precise."
    ],
    [
     "c12_3",
     {
      "label": "injector",
      "head": "Now: *fuel injectors*",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "injector"
      }
     },
     "Modern engines use injectors. Electric valves that spray a fine mist of fuel, many times a second."
    ],
    [
     "c12_4",
     {
      "label": "ecu",
      "head": "The *ECU* does the maths",
      "pose": "think",
      "face": "think",
      "prop": {
       "type": "injector",
       "ratio": true
      }
     },
     "The engine computer reads sensors, like how much air is coming in, and decides exactly how much fuel to spray."
    ],
    [
     "c12_5",
     {
      "label": "oxygen",
      "head": "The *oxygen sensor* checks the result",
      "pose": "count",
      "face": "smug",
      "prop": {
       "type": "injector"
      }
     },
     "An oxygen sensor in the exhaust checks the burn, and the computer fine tunes the mix constantly."
    ],
    [
     "c12_6",
     {
      "label": "direct",
      "head": "Port vs *direct* injection",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "grin",
      "prop": {
       "type": "versus",
       "a": {
        "t": "PORT",
        "big": "intake",
        "sub": "simpler"
       },
       "b": {
        "t": "DIRECT",
        "big": "cylinder",
        "sub": "more efficient"
       },
       "win": "b"
      }
     },
     "Port injection sprays into the intake. Direct injection sprays straight into the cylinder, at very high pressure, for better efficiency."
    ],
    [
     "c12_7",
